  "location": "Rhine gorge, a village above the river",
  "briefing": "The Rhine has been crossed elsewhere, and here the Americans mean to take it on the run. Two battalions cross in the morning mist, short of boats, shuttling over a few squads at a time. Above the bank waits a scratch German force built round a local headquarters: confused, short of fuel, but dug in, wired and hidden in the village and on the ridge behind it.",
